00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:18.000
And then

281
00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:21.600
importantly, you want to define some kind of grading rubric.

282
00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:22.560
So here this is.

283
00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:25.120
If you were to specify it for Tessl, you'll say

284
00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:26.480
what does a good solution look like.

285
00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:29.680
And you want to be pretty specific here so that you get reliable results

286
00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:30.400
from an LLM.

287
00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:33.960
So you'll say things like the solution should use this exact

288
00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:37.120
API call somewhere in the in the method,

289
00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:40.880
or it should implement or initialise this before it initialises that right.

